<!-- ══ 01 STRATEGY ══ -->
<section class="view on" id="v-strategy">
  <div class="masthead">
    <div class="eyebrow">Asia market penetration — pilot: Republic of Korea</div>
    <h1>You don't win Asia<br>by selling harder.</h1>
    <p class="lede">You win it by seeing the channel, buying the shelf, and owning the battery. MILWAUKEE® has the best professional tool on the market and 18% of the shelf. That gap is not a product problem — it is three structural problems, and every one of them is a data problem underneath.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pad">
    <div class="verbs">
      <div class="verb"><div class="vn">01</div><h3>See the channel</h3><p>Hundreds of independent distributors stand between MILWAUKEE® and the tradesman, ordering by WeChat, KakaoTalk and LINE in five languages. Sell-in is visible; sell-through is not.</p><p class="note">Modules 02–03</p></div>
